## 12.2 Example groundwater report workflow

If the selected location has evidence of low or declining groundwater:

1. Retrieve actual available groundwater measurements.
2. Inspect their dates and locations.
3. Check the measurement units.
4. Analyse historical changes.
5. Examine rainfall and drought context.
6. Examine available extraction and land-use information.
7. Review geological and hydrogeological context.
8. Identify nearby relevant facilities.
9. Cross-check relevant public environmental information.
10. Distinguish confirmed findings from hypotheses.
11. Identify additional measurements needed.
12. Generate practical conservation recommendations.

The report must not invent causes or assign blame without sufficient evidence.

